WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.717
An open-source Devin

00:00:01.529 --> 00:00:02.201
you can run

00:00:02.013 --> 00:00:02.779
yourself

00:00:03.294 --> 00:00:04.591
OpenComputer is an

00:00:04.402 --> 00:00:05.204
open-source

00:00:05.275 --> 00:00:06.548
self-hostable coding

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:07.562
agent for teams

00:00:07.702 --> 00:00:08.538
You mention it

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:09.093
in a Slack

00:00:08.904 --> 00:00:09.458
thread

00:00:09.624 --> 00:00:10.295
it works on

00:00:10.107 --> 00:00:11.156
its own computer

00:00:11.251 --> 00:00:11.982
and the result

00:00:11.794 --> 00:00:12.607
lands as a

00:00:12.419 --> 00:00:13.538
pull request

00:00:14.062 --> 00:00:15.076
The whole stack

00:00:14.923 --> 00:00:15.807
runs on one

00:00:15.619 --> 00:00:16.314
VM

00:00:16.453 --> 00:00:17.537
A gateway starts

00:00:17.349 --> 00:00:18.316
a Claude Code

00:00:18.375 --> 00:00:19.872
Codex or OpenCode

00:00:19.684 --> 00:00:20.273
session

00:00:20.545 --> 00:00:21.724
each isolated with

00:00:21.536 --> 00:00:22.879
rootless Podman

00:00:22.927 --> 00:00:23.740
and saved to

00:00:23.552 --> 00:00:24.719
a git-backed store

00:00:25.238 --> 00:00:25.969
It can run

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:26.405
in your own

00:00:26.217 --> 00:00:27.160
AWS

00:00:27.184 --> 00:00:28.339
Google Cloud or

00:00:28.163 --> 00:00:29.011
Azure account

00:00:29.141 --> 00:00:29.801
and the team

00:00:29.613 --> 00:00:30.473
says it opens

00:00:30.285 --> 00:00:31.924
pull requests 3.3

00:00:31.736 --> 00:00:32.950
times faster than

00:00:32.762 --> 00:00:33.587
Devin in its

00:00:33.398 --> 00:00:34.247
benchmark

00:00:34.782 --> 00:00:35.796
Full story on

00:00:35.607 --> 00:00:36.503
the dashboard
